          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most propane homes the <strong class="text-white">Rinnai RSC199iP</strong> is the one to buy: a dedicated LP model, condensing, recirculation capable and backed by the biggest service network. The <strong class="text-white">Noritz EZ111DV</strong> is the easiest swap from a tank, and the <strong class="text-white">Navien NPE-210A2</strong> is the pick when the wait for hot water is the real complaint.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before you buy any of them, settle the three things that decide whether it works: your winter temperature rise, whether your tank and regulator can supply the full BTU input, and where the vent goes. For camp showers, the <strong class="text-white">Eccotemp L5</strong> does the job, outdoors only.
